        "answer": {
          "short": "$Q_1=27$, median $=32$, $Q_3=38.5$, IQR $=11.5$.",
          "worked": "There are 24 values. The median is the average of the 12th and 13th values. Each half contains 12 values, so its median is the average of its 6th and 7th values.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Median}&=\\frac{32+32}{2}\\\\\\text{Median}&=32\\\\Q_1&=\\frac{27+27}{2}\\\\Q_1&=27\\\\Q_3&=\\frac{38+39}{2}\\\\Q_3&=38.5\\\\\\text{IQR}&=38.5-27\\\\\\text{IQR}&=11.5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
